==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Li'l Sexy Legs Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Li'l Macho Legs Cat''' when obtained from the [[Tiny Creeper (Deadly)|Li'l Gross Awakens! Stage]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
Due to being the Li'l version of a [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cat]], this unit suffers from a severe lack of good basic stats, making him underperform greatly in his field. For this reason, usage of Li'l Gross Cat prior to unlocking his [[True Form]] is not recommended.

==='''True Form'''===
Li'l Macho Legs Cat becomes a good stackable attacker for 4-Crown stages. It has enough health to be able to take some decently strong hits and enough attack power to hold its own against some enemies. However, his DPS prior to at a high level is unreliably low, so it's better to use better DPS dealers like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]]. Along with the added general use, the 30% knockback chance against [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] is a powerful asset in the right situation. If you can't keep back Aliens from your base, Li'l Macho Legs Cat is a viable no-[[:Category:Gacha Cats|gacha]] option, however, if you want a unit that can knockback Aliens, [[Ancient Egg: N105 (Rare Cat)|Racquet Cat]] performs better since she has higher health, faster speed and attack rate with better procs thanks to her [[Multi-Hit]].

His Barrier Breaker ability increases his usage greatly in [[Cats of the Cosmos]] and late [[Legend Stages]], allowing him to be relied upon for breaking the few [[Barrier]]s that can't easily be destroyed by normal attacks. Cats of the Cosmos features some stages with high-health barriers and a [[Restriction Stage|Special Only restriction]], where he will be a major help, but [[Skirt Cat (Special Cat)|Loincloth Cat]] may be better at exclusively breaking barriers due to range and stackability.

Despite all of this, Li'l Macho Legs still has shorter range and weaker health and attack power than the regular [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]], so he doesn't work well as a substitute.

==='''Talents'''===
With talents this cat can finally differentiate himself from his Manic and Normal counterparts, particularly due to his Shield Piercing talent. At max level he gains a 30% chance to pierce Aku Shields, being one of the only two easily obtainable shield piercing cats before beating the [[Aku Cyclone]], along with [[Li'l Jamiera Cat|Li'l Jamiera Cat.]] Though even with these merits, Li'l Macho Legs' long time between attacks, awful range and survivability doesn't justify the steep cost of obtaining this talent, even if it recharges faster than other Shield Piercers. With the introduction of [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]], [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]], this talent has lost much of its value, as they are all much stronger shield piercers than Li'l Macho Legs without requiring NP investment.

The curse resist talent is unnecessary, Li'l Macho Legs' low HP means he won't survive long enough against relic enemies to make use of it.
The Attack Buff and HP Buff talents, while helpful, are not necessary. Li'l Macho Legs has fairly low HP, and is more often used for his shield and barrier breaking abilities than his damage, making these talents that should not have a high priority. Avoid his Knockback Chance Up talent, as knocking back Aliens is generally not a good idea due to the sheer abundance of Alien backliners that will tear your army to shreds by pushing your backliners into their range.

==='''Orb'''===
Li'l Gross's lack of real general use means that giving it an orb should not be a priority by any means. Saying that, either the Cash Back or Death Mini-Surge Ability Orbs would be somewhat useful, for the general reasons why those two talent orbs are useful anyway, and Single Surge Counter could destroy the Barriers and Shields of entire crowds.

